.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt LIBAUDITCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm auditcmp_client_open ,
.Nm auditcmp_client_prepare ,
.Nm auditcmp_client_adopt ,
.Nm auditcmp_submit
.Nd authenticated BSM audit broker client
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In auditcmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn auditcmp_client_open "struct auditcmp_client **client"
.Ft int
.Fn auditcmp_submit "struct auditcmp_client *client" "const char *subject" "const char *operation" "int error"
.Ft void
.Fn auditcmp_client_close "struct auditcmp_client *client"
.In auditcmp_server.h
.Ft int
.Fn auditcmp_client_prepare "int *session_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn auditcmp_client_adopt "int session_fd" "struct auditcmp_client **client"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library submits bounded policy records to the privileged
.Xr auditbrokerd 8
service.
The provider maps the serviced-authenticated caller identity to a fixed BSM
event; clients cannot choose event numbers, audit user IDs, or provider
labels.
.Pp
.Fn auditcmp_client_prepare
creates a global service session configured to cross exactly one fork.
The child calls
.Fn auditcmp_client_adopt
before applying restrictions that prohibit incoming descriptor transfer.
The parent must close its copy after the fork.
.Fn auditcmp_client_adopt
always consumes
.Fa session_fd ,
including on failure.
.Pp
The preparation and adoption calls are provider bootstrap interfaces and are
therefore declared in
.In auditcmp_server.h ,
not the ordinary application header.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt int
return zero on success and \-1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr audit 2 ,
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr auditbrokerd 8
